{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri","id":1486518,"title":"What are your thoughts on the Salubri?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-15T07:01:46-07:00","id":1486518,"title":"What are your thoughts on the Salubri?","content":"IMHO, theyre alright. I dont really really see the exact need for them in the metaplot other than being the clan that got their Antedeluvian diablerized by Tremere to become a 3rd Gen. Maybe I'm being a bit too harsh. I like the stuff about Baali wars and Saluot. But other than that, I guess I just saw them as being there. I think the biggest reason I dont find them that intereting would have to be how it feels like they were only introduced because of the Tremere. Maybe I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-15-2022, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T07:19:26-07:00","id":1486520,"title":"","content":"I like options - and the Salubri present options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T07:30:27-07:00","id":1486521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486520#post1486520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like options - and the Salubri present options.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How often you pick that option?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T11:58:23-07:00","id":1486539,"title":"","content":"I've never used them and likely never will. My opinion on any bloodline is that they should only ever be introduced if the intention of the ST is for the PCs to explore the mystery of why that bloodline exists. The existing 13 clans already provide more than enough ground to cover almost any character concept they want, and probably 3 of these clans are already superfluous. Why have more unless they exist for a specific lore purpose?<br /> <br /> The only bloodline I've ever used in a game were those associated with the Cappadocian, and the &quot;mystery&quot; there is that the Cappadocians still exist. The Giovanni are full of themselves, and perhaps some time sooner than later, the Cappadocians will get their revenge. That plot line is actually played out now so in retrospect the Giovanni look entirely stupid. And I'm not sure how much of a mystery I could provide as ST since most players are going to know that by now. But as a result, the various lineages of the Cappadocians are figured out in my chronicles so they continue to get used in the setting though I don't follow the V5 version.<br /> <br /> But I've never figured out anything interesting to do with the other bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Now in an earlier thread, I reread the original clan description and came up with how I would run them. You can find that discussion starting <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450257-children-of-osiris/page4\">here</a>. The main points of how I would use them are 1) the magical number of seven Salubri exist for a reason, 2) Saulot intended these specific seven Salubri of eighth generation to survive, and 3) the diablerie they force their childer to perform on them is to ensure that each Salubri keeps adopting a new &quot;disguise&quot; every so often. As such, I'd never actually show these eighth generation Salubri in a chronicle lest they get killed. I'd only include their 9th generation childer who is still in the tutelage process of their master, but beginning to run their own blood cult around their master's ideals. That way if they get found and killed, it won't disrupt &quot;the master plan&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, while I think I could run individual scenes very effectively, I would still not use the Salubri in my own chronicles. Why? I still need to figure out exactly what the hell they are trying to do. Because a magical number of Salubri going around perpetuating their bloodline by diablerie is obviously doing these things for a reason. But what that reason is? No idea. I would want some vague conception at the minimum before doing using them. This has to be some very high Jyhad level stuff going on here. But an intriguing reason for it still escapes me. Until I do, they won't be showing up in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  fixed typo 07-22-2022, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T12:06:11-07:00","id":1486540,"title":"","content":"I don't have any thoughts about them and I probably will never play one in our game or even make a note of them as even existing. That is my two cents on the matter and since most of us are playing barely 200 year old monsters who are slowly learning the in and outs of our clan's histories and we wouldn't know about Saulot and his clan at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T12:38:08-07:00","id":1486545,"title":"","content":"They work great as Tremere antagonists, and I like the discipline spread. <br /> <br /> But, uh, a near-benevolent clan of vampires so nice that their weakness was that they couldn't drink blood without consent? Strictly Anti-Tremere propaganda. There's no way that could actually be a thing, and it doesn't fit the setting, at least how I run it. <br /> <br /> Warriors only: 10/10<br /> Healers: No thank you.<br /> Watchers: Bad<br /> African soul suckers- This works. <br /> <br /> <br /> The 7 or 8 salubri is a cool myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T13:14:42-07:00","id":1486548,"title":"","content":"I've barely used them. I've had a few Salubri-Antritribu be part of NPC packs, and that's about. I don't think I've had a single one do anything important enough to roll dice over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T14:31:27-07:00","id":1486554,"title":"","content":"Storytelling is like cooking; each clan is an ingredient and as such lends itself to specific cuisines and genres. But that also means that mixing some things together just doesn't work for every application.<br /> <br /> I have mostly used the Healer Salubri in my games rather than the other variants. But that was because I specifically wanted that almost extinct, non-combative, and moral quandary flavor in the given game. The Healer Salubri is also the default suggestion I have for any player who is really into roleplay and wants to do a drama heavy character, without needing to be the main character.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the restricted bloodline size and the potential for a &quot;hard mode&quot; survival build. Too many clans and bloodlines are more or less free for all's when it comes to numbers.<br /> <br /> As for the Tremere entanglement backstory... I see that less of a Salubri issue and more of a Tremere issue. White Wolf used the Tremere as the default plot point creator for so many things that it imbalanced the lore and the clans associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T16:17:10-07:00","id":1486558,"title":"","content":"I like the Salubri but I like them most when they're good guys but not the perfect victims of 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages: Salubri was the best Salubri.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T17:02:56-07:00","id":1486562,"title":"","content":"I like the old Warrior Salubri who functioned as religious zealots who went around killing evil things and things they claimed were evil. Never a big fan of the healer Salubri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T17:25:39-07:00","id":1486564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486558#post1486558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Salubri but I like them most when they're good guys but not the perfect victims of 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages: Salubri was the best Salubri.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree about DA Salubri.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T18:26:42-07:00","id":1486568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486562#post1486562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the old Warrior Salubri who functioned as religious zealots who went around killing evil things and things they claimed were evil. Never a big fan of the healer Salubri.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Healer Salubri but they needed that edge the Warrior Salubri said.<br /> <br /> The Salubri needed a balance between:<br /> <br /> * Perfect Saintly Vampire Kittens<br /> <br /> * Actually just the Baali and evil.<br /> <br /> For Healer Salubri, I would have added a bit of Mad Scientist and &quot;The Tzimisce and these guys often have fascinating conversations.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T19:00:24-07:00","id":1486570,"title":"","content":"I am currently running three games and they only feature in one of them, set in 5th century B.C.E. in Carthage. <br /> Because I dislike the Baali concept, and Infernalism as such, I have given the Healer Salubri an interesting role in the game. Their leader is a Mathuselah who believes that Clan affiliation and curses can be broken if they all submit to Baal Hammon, punic god of heaven and bestower of the blessing of vampirism upon the Dark Father. His end goal is to end the Antediluvians power to break the Jyhad and bring peace <br /> Sadly to hell is paved with good intentions and his project has become darker and darker as time goes by and their methods have gone beyond the questionable.<br /> This will eventually lead to the Roman Ventrue sacking Carthage. They will branded demon worshipers and thus the idea of Baali will be born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T19:39:02-07:00","id":1486572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486545#post1486545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, uh, a near-benevolent clan of vampires so nice that their weakness was that they couldn't drink blood without consent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like that for one reason - it explains why the clan was small enough so that they could get wiped out. There was never many of them. Embraces were few, and many did not work out. They didn't fit in with the rest of vampire society. That they didn't &quot;fit&quot; was exactly the point. Which is fine since they're not supposed to be a major part of the setting.<br /> <br /> Despite their appearance in the Players Guide, I never considered them a clan for one of the PCs. They are clearly meant to be NPCs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T20:17:27-07:00","id":1486574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486568#post1486568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like Healer Salubri but they needed that edge the Warrior Salubri said.<br /> <br /> The Salubri needed a balance between:<br /> <br /> * Perfect Saintly Vampire Kittens<br /> <br /> * Actually just the Baali and evil.<br /> <br /> For Healer Salubri, I would have added a bit of Mad Scientist and &quot;The Tzimisce and these guys often have fascinating conversations.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The big problem for me is that with the Healer Salubri, they have so much in-setting baggage that it's hard to actually use them. The weird &quot;there's only 7 of them and they allow their child to commit diablere on them,&quot; etc. They're so rare they don't make good PCs and also end up twisting the game around when you try and have them show up as NPCs. If they'd been more like a regular clan with larger numbers instead of being ultra-rare unicorns I'd like them a lot more. <br /> <br /> No coincidence the Warriors in the Sabbat are by far and away my favorite version of the Salubri because those guys are interesting and usable. The Wu-Zao/Watchers are kind of cool but again run into problems where they'd a bit hard to use at the table in the role of PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T20:21:55-07:00","id":1486575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486574#post1486574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big problem for me is that with the Healer Salubri, they have so much in-setting baggage that it's hard to actually use them. The weird &quot;there's only 7 of them and they allow their child to commit diablere on them,&quot; etc. They're so rare they don't make good PCs and also end up twisting the game around when you try and have them show up as NPCs. If they'd been more like a regular clan with larger numbers instead of being ultra-rare unicorns I'd like them a lot more.<br /> <br /> No coincidence the Warriors in the Sabbat are by far and away my favorite version of the Salubri because those guys are interesting and usable. The Wu-Zao/Watchers are kind of cool but again run into problems where they'd a bit hard to use at the table in the role of PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, it only takes one Healer Salubri to create a Bloodline of 9th to 13th generation.<br /> <br /> Someone who says, &quot;Screw this nonsense.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T21:01:27-07:00","id":1486577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486575#post1486575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true, it only takes one Healer Salubri to create a Bloodline of 9th to 13th generation.<br /> <br /> Someone who says, &quot;Screw this nonsense.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Feels like a quick way to get hunted down by the some of the other sects/clans if not done right. The sabbat would love to diablerize what they would see as hippies, and the followers of set may see the healers as a risk and try to eliminate them.<br /> <br /> The tremere probably wont get involved as they have already become a legitimate clan, and there would be nothing to gain by hunting a vampire bloodline that perfers to heal than fight.<br /> <br /> Camarilla probably wouldnt care, but the second someone starts flashing a 3rd eye they may make an example of the salubri in question. So buisness as usual.<br /> <br /> It feels like they would be just become another camarilla clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-16-2022, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T21:01:30-07:00","id":1486578,"title":"","content":"A waste of book pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T21:13:09-07:00","id":1486579,"title":"","content":"I don't like their concept of a whole Clan/Bloodline of &quot;good&quot; Cainites. They are as a bad as the Baali just from the other direction. And none of those two have a place as far as I'm concerned. The Salubri goes counter to the general themes and mood of the game and the Baali are over the top and everything they actually can be used for is done better by established Clans or Bloodlines of Cainites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T21:23:20-07:00","id":1486580,"title":"","content":"I think they have a little too much material on them.<br /> And goddamn, I'm a guy who really loves them.<br /> <br /> I would prefer if they got a &quot;thats it, thats how it is&quot; material, rather than a &quot;hey, those ten other supplements werent the entire true, actually the truee coonspiracy is that the Salubri have yet ANOTHEERE FUCKING BLOODLINE and Saulot has its fingers in yet another pie&quot;. <br /> <br /> Their concept is great. Martyrs, and ok, I accept having Warriors and Healers, it really drives that medieval feel they have (which is a shame that for most of Dark Ages they are... hunted, dead). I love Saulot's ambiguity, which yeah, can be quite a boring cobweb sometimes. The whole third eye... I think it makes people want to play them way too much just because of it. I wished it was a little more specific or situational, like the Banu Haqim darkening (although the Haquimites case for me is pretty darn stupid, and I'd rather have them have their skin losing color not for age, but because of diablerie; they're judges, it would make sense for them to show their 'true colors', and for the Path of Blood fellows would be a mark of dignity). <br /> <br /> The mindset Salubri have to have is pretty cool, if we are following a good willed one. Because surprise, you have to eat blood from people, hurt and drain them to continue. So... &quot;I'm hurting you so that I may continue to help you&quot;. A beast I am, lest a Beast I become. This way, even if you are playing a nice vampire it is still messed up. And there is so much room for villainy, hypocrisy, fanaticism, madness, despair, hate and anti-heroism in Salubris.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the end, they have tons of setting problems. Not only by playing one you are automatic in a hit list, but you weren't even supposed to be alive.<br /> Also, they always felt like the classic &quot;I'm different, I'm special, I'm awesome&quot; option, the magic dark elf with a hood from a massacred clan with unique Mary Sueisms. And you can't forget they are supposed to be rare and always hunted, so they don't even feel playable. They look awesome for a book, a novel, not a playable setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T22:09:50-07:00","id":1486585,"title":"","content":"A clan of victims needed to exist in order for the Tremere to have jumped over from Ars Magica and to have stolen vampirism without being demoted in status to membership in someone else's clan. They become interesting for the first and last time in Dark Ages, which coincided with Revised Edition and shared the core game's interest in deconstructing saints and anticipating the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Their V5 clan weakness, that it's hard to resist diablerizing them, is HILARIOUS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T22:32:19-07:00","id":1486587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486577#post1486577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feels like a quick way to get hunted down by the some of the other sects/clans if not done right. The sabbat would love to diablerize what they would see as hippies, and the followers of set may see the healers as a risk and try to eliminate them.<br /> <br /> The tremere probably wont get involved as they have already become a legitimate clan, and there would be nothing to gain by hunting a vampire bloodline that perfers to heal than fight.<br /> <br /> Camarilla probably wouldnt care, but the second someone starts flashing a 3rd eye they may make an example of the salubri in question. So buisness as usual.<br /> <br /> It feels like they would be just become another camarilla clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the best part because the Salubri are ALREADY hunted down by the Tremere like animals. They'll never be tolerated in Camarilla domains.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I originally thought the Salubri Antiribu were descended from Healers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486579#post1486579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like their concept of a whole Clan/Bloodline of &quot;good&quot; Cainites. They are as a bad as the Baali just from the other direction. And none of those two have a place as far as I'm concerned. The Salubri goes counter to the general themes and mood of the game and the Baali are over the top and everything they actually can be used for is done better by established Clans or Bloodlines of Cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's why they made the Baali into a bunch of Lovecraftian Cthulhu-tenders and the Followers of Set are finally breaking away from being the CLAN OF EVIL.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T22:37:28-07:00","id":1486589,"title":"","content":"My favorite clan, and they're as interesting as any clan with the same amount of development would be. That is, they depend a lot on you liking the basic concept because they're one of many Bloodlines that have been around for a long time but got a fraction of the page count of the main clans. If you only count Healers, they're more fleshed out than the Daughters of Cacophony and less than the Serpents of Light.<br /> <br /> For the metaplot, as far as it goes I think they're overused as plot devices instead of main characters, which is a big part of the aforementioned problem with little depiction. Saulot is a fleshed out character, almost, actually one of the better fleshed-out Antediluvian characters alongside with Cappadocius, for greater irony, but other than that they've been basically plot devices.<br /> <br /> That's to say that their lack of impression, especially when it comes to Metaplot, is less their fault (as in them being a boring idea) and more authorial decision (and not necessarily a bad or good decision, it just <b>is</b>). At the end of the day, for the purposes of the game, they are indeed a Bloodline and not a clan, meant more as options for distinct characters than as an actual main organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486521#post1486521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often you pick that option?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a player, about a third of my characters. As an ST, you can bet there will be one in the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T01:07:01-07:00","id":1486600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486575#post1486575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true, it only takes one Healer Salubri to create a Bloodline of 9th to 13th generation.<br /> <br /> Someone who says, &quot;Screw this nonsense.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but then you're still stuck playing that storyline out at the gaming table, which is awkward. Or making significant changes to the setting in order to have the Healer Salubri in a place where a player could reasonably play one without it being a particularly big deal in-setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T01:25:12-07:00","id":1486601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486600#post1486600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but then you're still stuck playing that storyline out at the gaming table, which is awkward. Or making significant changes to the setting in order to have the Healer Salubri in a place where a player could reasonably play one without it being a particularly big deal in-setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true.<br /> <br /> That is very much more a Storyteller or developer decision.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it'd be a very interesting Blood Cult. A bunch of Salubri in one city, feeding at a monastary or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T02:27:12-07:00","id":1486603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486601#post1486601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very true.<br /> <br /> That is very much more a Storyteller or developer decision.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it'd be a very interesting Blood Cult. A bunch of Salubri in one city, feeding at a monastary or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's a lot you could do.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles (that I was running even before V20) I had the Wu Zao travel to California to help the Kindred there in dealing with the Wan Kuei invasion. They brought a lot of magical knowledge and rituals that could help to contain the Wan Kuei. In exchange, the Anarchs agreed to protect the Wu Zao from the Camarilla (or rather the Tremere). One of the PCs was a Salubri Antitribu who was not part of the Sabbat. He was working with the the Wu Zao to engaging in dialogues with the Warrior Salubri in the Sabbat, with one of the eventual plot points being that they were going to convince many of the Warriors to leave the Sabbat. I was planning on having an outbreak of the Third Baali Wars happen with the Salubri (now having regained much of their lost clan lore) leading the charge against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T18:36:48-07:00","id":1486707,"title":"","content":"Really, with the Tremere breaking apart, it is prime time for chronicles with Salubri.<br /> Hell, you might want to throw out that it is all going according to Saulomere's wishes if you want that conspiratory 2nd and 3rd edition feel. Dead as they may be.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Warlocks aren't really in a position to be hunting relics of their past. They got way too many fresh problems. So it is perfect time for a Unicorns revival. Not saying that in a metaplot way, more in a table-by-table or game-by-game way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T18:41:19-07:00","id":1486708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486521#post1486521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How often you pick that option?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as often as I might like, mostly because I don't play VtM as much as I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:59:13-07:00","id":1486735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486587#post1486587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's why they made the Baali into a bunch of Lovecraftian Cthulhu-tenders and the Followers of Set are finally breaking away from being the CLAN OF EVIL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably although the wholesale removal of the Baali would have been even better. Still I very much like the changes done to the Setites.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T04:38:10-07:00","id":1486757,"title":"","content":"I appreciate their role in <i>Open your Eyes</i> in <i>Trails of Ash and Bone</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T06:22:53-07:00","id":1486763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486518-what-are-your-thoughts-on-the-salubri?p=1486574#post1486574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird &quot;there's only 7 of them and they allow their child to commit diablere on them,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they kinda &quot;fixed&quot; that back with the Players Guide to the High Clans, when introduced the Vengeful and flashed out the Seven a bit.<br /> But even before that several Salubri wandered around in WoD, the Islamic Salubri, known as the al-Amin (literally &quot;The Virtuous Ones&quot;), the &quot;honored guests' of the Ashirra, the Wu Zao &quot;Zao-lat's Family&quot; in the East, causing trouble for the Kuei-Jin (or even potentially start their Dharmic journey; tho that was just a gossip like note in Blood and Silk) and the Nkulu Zao in the Ebony Kingdom (Their very name is in honor of their founder; Nkulu Zao is Bavili for &quot;dead souls of Zao-lat&quot;.) who became genuine soul-suckers, taking the soul of any who threaten their safety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Vengeful</b>- This group is made up of Salubri who seek to avenge the great betrayal of their clan by fighting the Tremere and whoever allies himself with the Usurpers. It is a small group that suffers from great attrition. Recently, a young, charismatic Cainite calling himself Adonai has risen up to become a kind of leader of this group. He has become something of a hero among the Vengeful, but his abrasive and brusque behavior has alienated several of Europe\u2019s more powerful Cainites. Adonai is rumored to have discovered several fragments of the Code of Samiel, which in itself has rallied others to his banner. - PGtHC p.136. </div> </div> </div>As a sidenote, this Adonai probably the one who awoke and joined the Sabbat, forming the Antitiribu<br /> And the Seven:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Seven</b>- This is a group of seven Salubri on the Healer path. Heeding the old tales that Saulot often sought the. wisdom of Malkav, the Seven began to seek out old and powerful Malkavians and learn wisdom from them. In recent nights, the Seven have abandoned the battle against both the Baali and the Tremere and have instead begun a journey toward Golconda, espousing some rather bizarre ideas of salvation and diablerie to those of their fellows who have spoken with them. Apparently, these Seven believe that every Salubri should seek out Golconda, Embrace a worthy childe and then let this childe commit diablerie upon him.- PGtHC p.136. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the Malkavians &quot;bad influence&quot; made the Seven quite insane...<br /> <br /> Anyhow, later they tossed out the Seven-idea basically, making them the &quot;diversion&quot; so to speak, as we can see in Lore of the Bloodlines:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First thing\u2019s first: there are more than seven Salubri, let me assure you \u2014 and no, I\u2019m not counting antitribu in our number. Still, the Seven are by far the best-known representation of our Clan, and continue to succeed admirably in tainting the opinion of the Camarilla against us. They\u2019re a mixed blessing to the rest of the Clan: they draw a great deal of attention, but they also define our perception amongst the Kindred, as many hold their crimes against us. Their faults are not perhaps in their souls, but in themselves. I\u2019ll pass on more of my what sire taught me besides Shakespeare: when the Tremere hunts began to gain legitimacy during the War of Princes, seven elders of the Clan decided to follow in Saulot\u2019s footsteps, attempting to find enlightenment beyond the reach of the Usurpers. They followed the Silk Road to the East, ostensibly to find the Watchers and learn what secrets Saulot entrusted to them. They returned as deranged bodhisattvas, caretakers of a false Golconda. Embracing one childe apiece, then guiding that childe along the first steps to the Red Suspire, they urged their childer to commit diablerie upon them to eternally shepherd Raphael\u2019s Promise. The Seven believe they remain within the souls and blood of their diablerists, purifying rather than degrading. Besides acting as beacons for other seekers of Golconda or Tremere hunters, they frequently rip out the souls of mortals for their own inscrutable ends.On the one hand, they attacked my sire, Matthias of Bath, and attempted to diablerize him when he confronted them sometime around the Enlightenment. On the other hand, the neonate who nearly overpowered my sire showed incredible power and puissance for her age, with radiant veins in her aura instead of the pulsating black of diablerie. - Lore of the Bloodlines p.73. </div> </div> </div>Finally we have now a bit ambiguous description in V5, but enough to work with:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is whispered that only seven ever exist at one time, but whether or not that remains true in the modern nights cannot be confirmed. - V5 companion p.13. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I love the Salubri<br /> Tho' I think the V5 blood from the eye is a bit too much, but they are not just NPCs, the Salubi are just as playable as any other Clan/Bloodline if not more<br /> Heck, it is easier to play a Salubri than a Lasombra, Malkavian or Tzimisce with \u200borange and blue morality...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:30:44-07:00","id":1486874,"title":"","content":"This is something I have mentioned before in terms of the Salubri\u2026<br /> <br /> I think there is a misconception about what qualifies as good, particularly in terms of an RPG which depends on the agency and dynamism of the PCs. Good is not passive, well mannered, weak, or automatically a point of sacrifice. Morally good characters include Sam Vimes, Billy (of The Boys), and Dr. House. On a related note, I think Dr. House would make a good example of a Salubri and Dr. Lector would make a good example of Salubri Anti-Tribue. In any case, good should not mark a character as automatically lamb-like in a world of predators. For vampires, it should mean they do they best they can to remain moral and ethical in a world of sociopathic predators. <br /> <br /> So Salubri should not be goody-two shoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}